			],
			"Message": "style(Cocoon): Normalise esbuild config JS to 2-space indentation\n\nReformat all Configuration/ESBuild/*.js files and Configuration/Mountain/Config.js from tab indentation to consistent 2-space indentation, matching project conventions. Reorder import/export declarations for consistency across the config module tree — re-exports now appear before local imports, and duplicate/default import aliases are deduplicated (Target.js no longer re-imports TargetConfig under two aliases).\n\nRegenerate the RouteManifest timestamp and rebuild all Target/ compiled artifacts to reflect the reformatted configuration sources. No functional changes to build logic, RPC method registration (still 135 Mountain methods), or runtime behaviour.",
			"SHA": "986b90460fea5813aa884130c99e05ffe94c422a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T06:13:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1173,
				47
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Extract custom editor registration and registry maps into dedicated modules\n\nContinue the modularisation of the Window namespace by lifting the inline RegisterCustomEditor function into its own Source/Services/Handler/VscodeAPI/Window/RegisterCustomEditor.ts file and relocating all shared registry maps (CustomEditorProviders, CustomEditorProvidersByViewType, TreeDataProviders, TreeDataProvidersByViewId, WebviewViewProviders, WebviewViewBuilders, WebviewPanels) into a companion Registry.ts module. Namespace.ts now re-exports these maps and retains only the CreateWindowNamespace factory and its event subscriber helpers.\n\nThis follows the same extraction pattern applied to the extension host handler monolith in the previous commit, reducing Namespace.ts by roughly 170 lines of inline declarations. No functional changes to provider registration, lifecycle dispatch, or Mountain notification wiring.\n\nRegenerate all Target/ compiled artifacts and update the RouteManifest timestamp to reflect the new build.",
			"SHA": "d83ab1de7f16c00568710b5609626d80456c1268"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:37:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1164,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Extract extension host monolith into focused atomic modules\n\nSplit the 1500-line inline implementation in Handler.ts (InstallVscodeModuleHooks, EnsureVscodeAPIRegistered, ActivateExtension, CreateExtensionContext) into three dedicated files — VscodeModuleHooks.ts, EnsureVscodeAPI.ts, and ActivateExtension.ts — improving maintainability and reducing the extension host handler to a thin dispatch layer.\n\nAlongside the extraction, fix several real-world extension compatibility issues:\n- ActivateExtension.ts: Add fs preflight check before importing main bundle (skips Copilot and other extensions whose dist files are absent from source checkouts); populate `context.extension.packageJSON` from the real manifest on disk so `@vscode/extension-telemetry` reads `aiKey`; seed workspace config cache from the extension's `contributes.configuration.properties` before activate() runs (prevents GitLens TypeError on nested config access); backfill `activate()` return value into the registry entry so `vscode.extensions.getExtension(id).exports` resolves correctly; use the real VS Code URI class when available to avoid `URI.joinPath` errors\n- EnsureVscodeAPI.ts: Add POJO-tolerant RelativePattern wrapper (fixes Shopify.ruby-lsp activation); add missing VS Code API enums (LogLevel, OverviewRulerLane, UIKind, TextEditorCursorStyle, DebugConfigurationProviderTriggerKind, IndentAction) that the extHostTypes spread misses — extensions referencing them at module-load time crashed with undefined\n- VscodeModuleHooks.ts: (carried forward, no functional change)\n- Notification handler: Fix `willSaveTextDocument` — collect all `waitUntil` thenables and batch returned TextEdits into a single `window.applyTextEdits` call instead of forwarding eagerly per-thenable, matching VS Code's `acceptWillSaveDocument` ordering\n- Configuration cache: Support `\"*\"` sentinel for full model rebuild — wipe and re-prime cached keys on settings.json writes that affect many keys at once",
			"SHA": "e4175f34918950d520c425f71d9878afdaeb3d70"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:21:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1161,
				3
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Keep extension-observable state live in workspace, terminals, and diagnostics\n\nReplace multiple stale or empty state placeholders in the Cocoon extension host with live-tracking counterparts that extensions actually query at runtime.\n\nURI robustness: MakeUriStub provides a minimal URI-like object when LazyURI.parse fails, preventing folders from being silently dropped from the workspace list.\n\nVisible text editors: Track the active editor in `__visibleTextEditors`, upsert on `didChangeTextEditorSelection`, and filter on `$acceptModelRemoved` so iterators (GitLens, Error Lens, formatters) see real open-editor state instead of a static empty array.\n\nTerminals: `createTerminal` now pushes into `__terminals` and sets `__activeTerminal`, with proper cleanup on dispose. The `terminals` and `activeTerminal` properties are getters backed by these arrays.\n\nDiagnostics: Introduce a module-level `_AllDiagnostics` cache that mirrors every DiagnosticCollection.set/delete/clear call. `getDiagnostics()` now returns real aggregated diagnostics across owners instead of an empty array, and emits `diagnostics.didChange` events so downstream consumers can react to diagnostic updates without an async Mountain round-trip.",
			"SHA": "6a1ecbf53b069944bb7ca27fd9361fa86a8a8d4d"
		}
	],
